  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two charges of each magnitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and&nbsp;separated by a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> constitute an&nbsp;electric dipole. If the dipole is placed in an uniform&nbsp;electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>dyne</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> making <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math> angle with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the magnitude of torque acting on dipole is:</p>"
  },
